# ThreadSanitizer suppressions.
#
# The distro libgrpc/libgpr are NOT built with -fsanitize=thread, so TSan cannot see the
# synchronisation gRPC performs internally and reports false races on its own epoll state.
# These suppressions are deliberately narrow: they match only gRPC's event-engine poller
# symbols. We do NOT use `called_from_lib:libgrpc`, because our service handlers run on gRPC
# threads and every race in them would then be hidden too.
race:grpc_event_engine::posix_engine::Epoll1Poller
# gRPC client call ops: the request/response buffers are moved between the calling thread and
# gRPC's default-executor thread inside libgrpc (visible after a channel reconnect). Both stacks
# are gRPC-internal; our own request objects are local to the calling thread.
race:grpc::internal::CallOpSet
# gRPC reconnect path: TCP connector state shared between gRPC's event-engine and global-timer
# threads. The stacks contain no Kestrel frames at all.
race:grpc_tcp_client_create_from_prepared_fd
# POLICY: a report that has a kestrel:: frame is never suppressed; it gets fixed.
